error[E0277]: `u8` cannot be encrypted into one `Ciphertext`
  --> tests/ui/owned_collection_elements.rs:11:26
   |
11 |     let _ = vec![1u8, 2].encrypt_into::<Vec<Ciphertext>, _>(keyset);
   |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this must be one owned value that can be wiped
   |
   = help: the trait `stack_encrypt::scalar::sealed::OneValue` is not implemented for `u8`
   = note: to be encrypted into one `Ciphertext`, a value must meet three conditions.
   = note: first, the value must be one scalar or an `OpaqueBlob<T>`. A scalar is a value such as a `String`, a `bool`, a float, a `Vec<u8>`, or a fixed-width integer other than `u8`. A newtype that derives `Encrypt` over a scalar is a scalar too.
   = note: second, the value must be owned. A borrow, such as a `&str`, is not owned.
   = note: third, the type must implement `Zeroize`, so that the value can be wiped after it is encrypted. For an `OpaqueBlob<T>`, `T` must implement `Zeroize` and `Serialize`.
   = note: these calls encrypt a value that is not one scalar. `EncryptInto` encrypts each element of a `Vec` into its own `Ciphertext`. `keyset.encrypt_tree` encrypts an `Option` or a struct into a tree of ciphertexts. `OpaqueBlob` encrypts a whole `Serialize` value into one `Ciphertext`.
help: the trait `EncryptTarget<Vec<S>>` is implemented for `Vec<T>`
  --> src/target/collections.rs
   |
   | / impl<S: Zeroize, T: EncryptTarget<S>> EncryptTarget<Vec<S>> for Vec<T>
   | | where
   | |     T::ContextInput: Clone + MaybeSend + 'static,
   | |_________________________________________________^
   = note: required for `u8` to implement `OpaqueEncode`
   = note: required for `stack_encrypt::Ciphertext` to implement `EncryptTarget<u8>`
   = note: 1 redundant requirement hidden
   = note: required for `Vec<stack_encrypt::Ciphertext>` to implement `EncryptTarget<Vec<u8>>`

